<link rel="stylesheet" href="/s-hhkzs.css"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://vexcura.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Academic EHR comparison","item":"https://vexcura.com/academic-ehr-comparison"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is an academic EHR?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An academic (or educational) EHR is a practice electronic health record built for teaching. Nursing students chart on made-up patients, with medication records, flowsheets, orders and care plans, so they learn documentation before they use a hospital's live system. It holds no real patient records."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are some alternatives to SimChart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Academic EHRs used in nursing education include Elsevier SimChart, EHR Go, Lippincott DocuCare and Vexcura. The table on this page lists what each one publishes about price, who pays and what it includes, with sources and dates. Ask each vendor for a demo and a current quote, since prices and plans change."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does EHR Go cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"EHR Go's FAQ lists student subscriptions from $53 for 12 weeks to $293 for 36 months, including $73 for a 16-week semester and $128 for 12 months (checked November 16, 2026). It says faculty access is free and that schools buying 200 or more subscriptions get a volume discount."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do nursing students pay for an academic EHR?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often they do. EHR Go says students can buy subscriptions online or in the bookstore, and Lippincott sells DocuCare access on its store. Some schools buy access for students or include it in a course fee. With Vexcura, the school licenses it, students and instructors never pay, and every nursing student can also create a free account on their own."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Vexcura's academic EHR like Epic?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It's Epic-style: the layout follows charting patterns students meet in hospital systems, such as a patient summary, a MAR on a time ruler, flowsheets and a worklist sidebar. Vexcura isn't affiliated with or endorsed by Epic Systems Corporation and doesn't copy its software."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Vexcura include more than the EHR?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every plan includes the academic EHR, NCLEX-RN practice questions and adaptive practice exams, clinical simulations, the clinical instructor workspace with attendance and badge sign-in, curriculum uploads, Google and Microsoft sign-in and LTI 1.3 for your LMS. Plans differ only by how many students they cover."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can we try Vexcura before we switch?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A free one-semester pilot covers one clinical group or cohort, with no obligation to buy. Faculty accounts are always free, so instructors can look around before the pilot starts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can we keep our current EHR during a pilot?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Vexcura runs in a web browser and doesn't need to connect to another EHR product, so a program can pilot it with one clinical group while the rest of its courses stay on their current academic EHR."}}]}</script></head><body><header class="top"><div class="w"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Vexcura home"><svg class="vxw" viewBox="-2 -86 472 96" aria-hidden="true"><defs><linearGradient id="sxlW" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="0" y1="0" x2="227.0" y2="0"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:var(--vxa);stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset=".5" style="stop-color:var(--vxb);stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:1"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="sxlWr" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="0" y1="0" x2="227.0" y2="0"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:#ffffff;stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset=".5" style="stop-color:var(--vxrb);stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxrc);stop-opacity:1"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="sxlB" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="16" y1="-72" x2="27" y2="4"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:var(--vxb);stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:1"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="sxlBr" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="16" y1="-72" x2="27" y2="4"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:#ffffff;stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxrc);stop-opacity:1"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="sxlF" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="0" y1="4" x2="25" y2="-72"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:0"/><stop offset=".55" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:0.55"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:0.95"/></linearGradient></defs><path class="bmf" d="M14 -72h11L11 4H0z" fill="url(#sxlF)"/><path class="bmb" d="M30 -72h11L27 4H16z" fill="url(#sxlB)"/><g transform="translate(50 0)"><path d="M47.1 0L21.5 0L9.3-68.8L32.1-68.8L36-37Q36.2-35.7 36.5-33.2Q36.8-30.7 37.1-27.9Q37.5-25.1 37.8-22.8L37.8-22.8L38.2-22.8Q39.4-25.2 40.5-27.6Q41.6-29.9 42.8-32.3Q43.9-34.7 45-37L45-37L60.2-68.8L83.6-68.8L47.1 0ZM97.1 1.2L97.1 1.2Q88.5 1.2 82.3-1.2Q76.1-3.5 72.8-8.3Q69.4-13.2 69.4-20.7L69.4-20.7Q69.4-22.9 69.5-25.0Q69.7-27 70.1-28.9L70.1-28.9Q71.6-37.3 76.1-42.9Q80.6-48.4 87.5-51.2Q94.3-54 102.6-54L102.6-54Q111.3-54 117.3-51.8Q123.4-49.6 126.5-45.1Q129.7-40.5 129.7-33.4L129.7-33.4Q129.7-31.8 129.5-29.6Q129.3-27.4 128.5-23L128.5-23L88.9-23L88.7-21.3Q88.5-20.2 88.5-19.4L88.5-19.4Q88.5-16.9 89.4-15.1Q90.3-13.3 92.3-12.4Q94.3-11.5 97.4-11.5L97.4-11.5Q100.1-11.5 102.0-12.1Q104-12.7 105.3-13.8Q106.6-14.8 107.4-16.2Q108.2-17.6 10