   </div></details></nav></div></header><script>(function(){var d=document.querySelector(".mnav");if(!d)return;document.addEventListener("click",function(e){if(d.open&&!d.contains(e.target))d.open=false});document.addEventListener("keydown",function(e){if(e.key==="Escape"&&d.open){d.open=false;d.querySelector("summary").focus()}})})();</script><main><nav class="crumb w" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <span>Academic EHR comparison</span></nav><section class="hero w"><h1>Academic EHR Comparison: SimChart Alternatives for Nursing Schools</h1><p class="lead">What Elsevier SimChart, EHR Go, Lippincott DocuCare and Vexcura publish about price, who pays and what each includes, with sources and dates. Then estimate the cost for your program and use the checklist to compare vendors.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="#ehr-calc">Estimate your cost</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools#pilot">Request a free semester pilot</a></div></section><div class="w"><style>
.vx-val{margin:34px 0}.vx-val h2{margin-top:0}
.vx-cmp{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,230px),1fr));gap:12px;margin:16px 0}
.vx-cmp>div{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;display:grid;gap:4px;align-content:start}
.vx-cmp b{font:400 20px/1.2 var(--fh)}.vx-cmp .amt{font:700 24px/1.2 var(--fb);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ink)}.vx-cmp small{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;line-height:1.4}
.vx-cmp .vx-us{background:var(--navy);border-color:var(--navy);color:var(--navy-ink)}.vx-cmp .vx-us .amt,.vx-cmp .vx-us b{color:var(--navy-ink)}.vx-cmp .vx-us small{color:var(--navy-ink);opacity:.85}
.vx-calc{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-top:4px solid var(--gold);border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px;margin:18px 0}
.vx-calc h3{margin:0 0 8px}.vx-calc .vc-in{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 16px;align-items:center}.vx-calc label{font-weight:700}
.vx-calc input[type=range]{flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0;accent-color:var(--accent)}.vx-calc input[type=number]{width:96px;font:17px var(--fb);padding:7px 9px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink)}
.vx-calc fieldset{border:0;padding:0;margin:10px 0 0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 18px}.vx-calc legend{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:4px;padding:0}.vx-calc fieldset label{font-weight:400;display:inline-flex;gap:6px;align-items:center}
.vx-out{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,200px),1fr));gap:10px;margin:14px 0 4px}.vx-out>div{background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px}
.vx-out span{display:block;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.vx-out output{display:block;font:700 22px/1.25 var(--fb);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.vx-out small{color:var(--muted)}
.vx-note{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:6px 0 0}
.vx-ps{max-width:520px}.vx-ps td:nth-child(n+3),.vx-ps th:nth-child(n+3){text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}
.vx-scale{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(100%,220px),1fr));gap:8px 18px;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:12px 0}.vx-scale li{line-height:1.35}.vx-scale b{color:var(--accent)}
.vx-fn{font-size:14px}.vx-fn td,.vx-fn th{padding:6px 8px}.vx-fn a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}
.vx-strip{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:5px solid var(--gold);border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px;margin:30px 0}
.vx-strip h2{font-size:clamp(22px,3.2vw,28px);margin:0 0 6px}.vx-strip ul{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:10px 0}
.vx-strip li{background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:14.5px}.vx-strip li b{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.vx-strip p{margin:6px 0}</style>
    <h2 id="compare">Academic EHRs for nursing schools at a glance</h2>
    <div class="tw"><table class="cmp"><thead><tr><th>Academic EHR</th><th>Who usually pays</th><th>Published price</th><th>What the vendor lists</th></tr></thead><tbody>
     <tr><td><b>Elsevier SimChart</b></td><td data-l="Who usually pays">Not stated on the store page<sup><a href="#ehr-src-0">1</a></sup></td><td data-l="Published price">No price shown on Elsevier's store page<sup><a href="#ehr-src-0">1</a></sup></td><td data-l="What the vendor lists">A blank charting tool, a pre-clinical manager for researching diagnoses, medications and tests, pre-built unfolding case studies including 60 introductory cases, and assignments mapped to the nursing curriculum<sup><a href="#ehr-src-0">1</a></sup></td></tr>
     <tr><td><b>EHR Go</b></td><td data-l="Who usually pays">Students, online or in the bookstore; schools can also buy subscriptions, with a volume discount from 200. Free for faculty<sup><a href="#ehr-src-1">2</a></sup></td><td data-l="Published price">$53 (12 weeks) to $293 (36 months); $73 per 16-week semester; $128 for 12 months<sup><a href="#ehr-src-1">2</a></sup></td><td data-l="What the vendor lists">Hundreds of documentation forms, such as orders, problem lists, vital signs, labs and care plans; patient cases faculty can copy and edit in a private library; interprofessional use<sup><a href="#ehr-src-1">2</a></sup></td></tr>
     <tr><td><b>Lippincott DocuCare</b></td><td data-l="Who usually pays">Students, through the Lippincott store or a bookstore<sup><a href="#ehr-src-2">3</a></sup>; some schools fold it into a course fee with other Lippincott products<sup><a href="#ehr-src-3">4</a></sup></td><td data-l="Published price">$71.99 for 6 months of standalone access<sup><a href="#ehr-src-2">3</a></sup></td><td data-l="What the vendor lists">An educational EHR sold standalone or bundled with other Lippincott products<sup><a href="#ehr-src-3">4</a></sup></td></tr>
     <tr><td><b>Vexcura</b></td><td data-l="Who usually pays">The school licenses it; students and instructors never pay, and every nursing student can also create a free account</td><td data-l="Published price">From $199 per student seat per year, or site plans by program size (<a href="/for-nursing-schools#pricing">pricing</a>). A free one-semester pilot covers one clinical group or cohort, with no obligation to buy.</td><td data-l="What the vendor lists">An Epic-style academic EHR (My Chart, MAR with barcode scanning of practice wristbands and medications, spreadsheet-style flowsheets, orders, the LDA avatar, care plans, SBAR handoff, SDOH screening, Secure Chat), a case library, live clinical groups, LTI 1.3 grade sync, plus NCLEX-RN practice and simulations in the same license</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p class="src" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px">Typical published prices on the dates shown; your costs may differ. Institutional contract prices are often not public, so ask each vendor for a current quote. SimChart is a trademark of Elsevier, EHR Go of its owner, and DocuCare and Lippincott of Wolters Kluwer. Vexcura isn't affiliated with or endorsed by any of them.</p>
    <div class="vx-calc" id="ehr-calc" data-ec='{&quot;go&quot;:[[&quot;16 weeks (one semester)&quot;,73,1],[&quot;40 weeks (academic year)&quot;,113,1],[&quot;12 months&quot;,128,1],[&quot;24 months&quot;,203,2],[&quot;36 months&quot;,293,3]],&quot;seat&quot;:199,&quot;seatName&quot;:&quot;Per student&quot;,&quot;sites&quot;:[{&quot;n&quot;:&quot;Site 100&quot;,&quot;p&quot;:15000,&quot;m&quot;:100},{&quot;n&quot;:&quot;Site 250&quot;,&quot;p&quot;:30000,&quot;m&quot;:250},{&quot;n&quot;:&quot;Site 500&quot;,&quot;p&quot;:50000,&quot;m&quot;:500}],&quot;cap&quot;:500,&quot;custom&quot;:&quot;Custom quote&quot;}'><h3>Estimate what an academic EHR costs, and who pays</h3>
    <div class="vc-in"><label for="ec-n">Number of students</label><input type="range" id="ec-r" min="10" max="500" step="5" value="60" aria-label="Number of students"><input type="number" id="ec-n" min="1" max="1000" value="60" inputmode="numeric"></div>
    <fieldset><legend>Access needed</legend><label><input type="radio" name="ec-t" value="0"> 16 weeks (one semester)</label><label><input type="radio" name="ec-t" value="1"> 40 weeks (academic year)</label><label><input type="radio" name="ec-t" value="2"> 12 months</label><label><input type="radio" name="ec-t" value="3" checked> 24 months</label><label><input type="radio" name="ec-t" value="4"> 36 months</label></fieldset>
    <fieldset><legend>Who buys the EHR Go subscriptions</legend><label><input type="checkbox" id="ec-s"> The school buys them (volume discount from 200)</label></fieldset>
    <div class="vx-out" aria-live="polite"><div><span>EHR Go, published price</span><output id="ec-g">—</output><small id="ec-gp">—</small></div><div><span>Vexcura license</span><output id="ec-v">—</output><small id="ec-vp">—</small></div><div><span>What students pay for Vexcura</span><output>$0</output><small>students and instructors are free</small></div></div>
    <p class="vx-note">An estimate from published prices (EHR Go FAQ, checked November 16, 2026; Vexcura plans from its pricing page); your costs may differ, and taxes, bookstore markups and negotiated contracts aren't included. The Vexcura license also covers NCLEX-RN practice, simulations and instructor tools, and is licensed per year. Elsevier doesn't show a SimChart price on its store page, so it isn't in the estimate.</p></div>
    <script>(function(){var w=document.getElementById("ehr-calc");if(!w)return;var C=JSON.parse(w.getAttribute("data-ec")),r=w.querySelector("#ec-r"),n=w.querySelector("#ec-n"),s=w.querySelector("#ec-s");
    function m(x){return "$"+Math.round(x).toLocaleString("en-US")}
    function best(k){var o=[];if(C.seat)o.push({n:C.seatName,t:C.seat*k});C.sites.forEach(function(x){if(x.m>=k)o.push({n:x.n,t:x.p})});o.sort(function(a,b){return a.t-b.t});return o[0]}
    function go(src){var k=Math.max(1,Math.round(+(src||n).value||0));if(src===r)n.value=k;else r.value=Math.min(C.cap,Math.max(10,k));
     var t=w.querySelector('input[name="ec-t"]:checked'),g=C.go[t?+t.value:3],d=s.checked&&k>=200?Math.min(25,5+Math.floor((k-200)/100)):0,tot=g[1]*k*(1-d/100);
     w.querySelector("#ec-g").textContent=m(tot);w.querySelector("#ec-gp").textContent=m(g[1]*(1-d/100))+" per student for "+g[0]+(d?" ("+d+"% volume discount)":"")+"; paid by "+(s.checked?"the school":"students");
     var b=k>C.cap?null:best(k),v=w.querySelector("#ec-v"),vp=w.querySelector("#ec-vp");
     if(!b){v.textContent=C.custom;vp.textContent="More than "+C.cap+" students";return}
     v.textContent=m(b.t*g[2]);vp.textContent=b.n+" · "+m(b.t)+" per year"+(g[2]>1?" × "+g[2]+" years":"")+"; paid by the school"}
    r.addEventListener("input",function(){go(r)});n.addEventListener("input",function(){go(n)});s.addEventListener("change",function(){go(n)});w.querySelectorAll('input[name="ec-t"]').forEach(function(c){c.addEventListener("change",function(){go(n)})});go(n)})();</script>
    <h2 id="choose">How to choose an academic EHR: questions to ask every vendor</h2>
    <ol><li><b>Who pays, and for how long?</b> Per-student subscriptions often end with the access period, so check what a student needs across the whole program.</li><li><b>Does it look like what students will chart on in clinicals?</b> A MAR on a time ruler, flowsheets in time columns and a worklist make the first clinical day less of a shock.</li><li><b>Can faculty build and edit cases?</b> And can you upload your own course content beside the vendor's?</li><li><b>Can instructors see student charts and grade them?</b> Look for read-only clinical groups and grades that go back to your LMS.</li><li><b>How does it keep real patient data out?</b> Practice charts shouldn't have fields for names, dates of birth or record numbers.</li><li><b>Can you pilot it with one group first?</b> A semester with one clinical group shows more than a demo.</li></ol>
    <h2>How Vexcura answers those questions</h2>
    <div class="feat"><div><b>Students never pay</b>The school licenses Vexcura; students and instructors are free, and every plan includes everything.</div><div><b>Charting that feels familiar</b>My Chart, a MAR that flags due and overdue doses, spreadsheet-style flowsheets and a worklist sidebar, on made-up patients.</div><div><b>Your cases and content</b>Assign from the case library or save your own versions, and upload your own curriculum into the same Library.</div><div><b>Instructors see the work</b>Students share practice patients with a live clinical group, instructors see them read-only, and assigned cases are graded from the chart.</div><div><b>Your LMS</b>LTI 1.3 for Canvas, Blackboard, D2L Brightspace and Moodle, with grades sent back, plus Google and Microsoft sign-in. Vexcura hasn't completed 1EdTech certification yet.</div><div><b>Real data kept out</b>Hospital days instead of dates, no name or record-number fields, ages over 89 shown as 90+, and a warning when something looks like an identifier.</div></div>
    <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>vexcura.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/d-mar-1000.webp" srcset="/img/d-mar-1600.webp 1600w, /img/d-mar-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="Academic EHR medication administration record on a made-up patient, with 0900 doses due, a hold parameter and a high-alert flag" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>Vexcura's MAR on a made-up practice patient: 0900 doses due.</figcaption></figure>
    <p>See every charting feature on the <a href="/academic-ehr-for-nursing-students">academic EHR page</a>, or <a href="/for-nursing-schools#pilot">request a free semester pilot</a>.</p>
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><h3>What is an academic EHR?</h3><p>An academic (or educational) EHR is a practice electronic health record built for teaching. Nursing students chart on made-up patients, with medication records, flowsheets, orders and care plans, so they learn documentation before they use a hospital's live system. It holds no real patient records.</p><h3>What are some alternatives to SimChart?</h3><p>Academic EHRs used in nursing education include Elsevier SimChart, EHR Go, Lippincott DocuCare and Vexcura. The table on this page lists what each one publishes about price, who pays and what it includes, with sources and dates. Ask each vendor for a demo and a current quote, since prices and plans change.</p><h3>How much does EHR Go cost?</h3><p>EHR Go's FAQ lists student subscriptions from $53 for 12 weeks to $293 for 36 months, including $73 for a 16-week semester and $128 for 12 months (checked November 16, 2026). It says faculty access is free and that schools buying 200 or more subscriptions get a volume discount.</p><h3>Do nursing students pay for an academic EHR?</h3><p>Often they do. EHR Go says students can buy subscriptions online or in the bookstore, and Lippincott sells DocuCare access on its store. Some schools buy access for students or include it in a course fee. With Vexcura, the school licenses it, students and instructors never pay, and every nursing student can also create a free account on their own.</p><h3>Is Vexcura's academic EHR like Epic?</h3><p>It's Epic-style: the layout follows charting patterns students meet in hospital systems, such as a patient summary, a MAR on a time ruler, flowsheets and a worklist sidebar. Vexcura isn't affiliated with or endorsed by Epic Systems Corporation and doesn't copy its software.</p><h3>Does Vexcura include more than the EHR?</h3><p>Yes. Every plan includes the academic EHR, NCLEX-RN practice questions and adaptive practice exams, clinical simulations, the clinical instructor workspace with attendance and badge sign-in, curriculum uploads, Google and Microsoft sign-in and LTI 1.3 for your LMS. Plans differ only by how many students they cover.</p><h3>Can we try Vexcura before we switch?</h3><p>A free one-semester pilot covers one clinical group or cohort, with no obligation to buy. Faculty accounts are always free, so instructors can look around before the pilot starts.</p><h3>Can we keep our current EHR during a pilot?</h3><p>Yes. Vexcura runs in a web browser and doesn't need to connect to another EHR product, so a program can pilot it with one clinical group while the rest of its courses stay on their current academic EHR.</p></div>
    <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2><ol class="os-src"><li id="ehr-src-0">Elsevier, <a href="https://shop.elsevier.com/books/simchart-next-generation/elsevier-inc/978-0-443-11323-9" rel="nofollow noopener">SimChart Next Generation (store page)</a> (Checked November 16, 2026).</li><li id="ehr-src-1">EHR Go, <a href="https://ehrgo.com/faq/" rel="nofollow noopener">Frequently asked questions (prices, who buys, faculty access)</a> (Checked November 16, 2026).</li><li id="ehr-src-2">Wolters Kluwer (Lippincott), <a href="https://shop.lww.com/p/9781451187182" rel="nofollow noopener">Lippincott DocuCare, 6-month access (store)</a> (Accessed November 4, 2026).</li><li id="ehr-src-3">University of Maryland School of Nursing, <a href="https://www.nursing.umaryland.edu:443/media/son/admissions/School-Specific-Fee-Explanation-FY24-SON.pdf" rel="nofollow noopener">School-specific fee explanation, FY24 (DocuCare in a bundled clinical fee)</a> (FY24).</li></ol>
    <p class="src" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px">Vendor details are paraphrased from the public pages listed above and may have changed since. Epic is a trademark of Epic Systems Corporation; "Epic-style" describes a familiar layout, not a copy of any vendor's software. Vexcura is independent and isn't affiliated with or endorsed by any EHR vendor.</p><h2>Related</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/academic-ehr-for-nursing-students">Epic-style academic EHR</a></li><li><a href="/for-nursing-schools">Vexcura for nursing schools</a></li><li><a href="/nursing-simulation-scenarios">Nursing simulation scenarios and drills</a></li><li><a href="/software">The Vexcura platform</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-prep-comparison">NCLEX prep compared</a></li></ul></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Free for every nursing student</h2><p>Create an account and get the full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam, 1,220 cited questions, 8 NGN case studies, the Epic-style academic EHR and the simulations, with or without a school. Nursing programs license Vexcura for their cohorts and faculty, and every plan includes everything.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/app#signup" data-cta="band">Create your free account</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools">For nursing schools</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot mktf"><div class="w">
